%I A194687 #46 Oct 03 2026 16:30:06
%S A194687 1,5,34,1254,29274,48272239,6611719866,797507543735
%N A194687 Least k such that the rank of the elliptic curve y^2 = x^3 - k^2*x is n, or -1 if no such k exists.
%C A194687 Fermat found a(0), Biling found a(1), and Wiman found a(2)-a(4). Rogers found upper bounds on a(5) and a(6) equal to their true value; Rathbun and an unknown author verified them as a(5) and a(6), respectively.
%C A194687 Rogers (2004) found an upper bound on a(7) equal to its true value; Kenjaev (2026) proved that it is exact. - _Otakhon U. Kenjaev_, Sep 29 2026
%D A194687 G. Billing, "Beiträge zur arithmetischen theorie der ebenen kubischen kurven geschlechteeins", Nova Acta Reg. Soc. Sc. Upsaliensis (4) 11 (1938), Nr. 1. Diss. 165 S.
%D A194687 N. Rogers, "Elliptic curves x^3 + y^2 = k with high rank", PhD Thesis in Mathematics, Harvard University (2004).
%D A194687 A. Wiman, "Über rationale Punkte auf Kurven y^2 = x(x^2-c^2)", Acta Math. 77 (1945), pp. 281-320.
%H A194687 Andrej Dujella, Ali S. Janfada, and Sajad Salami, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL12/Janfada/janfada3.html">A search for high rank congruent number elliptic curves</a>, Journal of Integer Sequences, Vol. 12 (2009), Article 09.5.8.
%H A194687 Otakhon U. Kenjaev, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23028371">The smallest congruent number curve of rank seven</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A194687 Randall L. Rathbun, <a href="https://listserv.nodak.edu/cgi-bin/wa.exe?A2=NMBRTHRY;16b991d8.1108">Posting to NMBRTHRY</a>, Aug 25 2011.
%H A194687 N. F. Rogers, <a href="https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.em/1045759524">Rank computations for the congruent number elliptic curves</a>, Exper. Math. 9:4 (2000), pp. 591-594.
%H A194687 K. Rubin and A. Silverberg, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1090/S0273-0979-02-00952-7">Ranks of elliptic curves</a>, Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. 39 (2002), 455-474, p.464, Table 2.
%H A194687 Mark Watkins, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5802/jtnb.653">On elliptic curves and random matrix theory</a>, Journal de Theorie des Nombres de Bordeaux, Tome 20 (2008) no. 3, pp. 829-845.
%H A194687 Author?, <a href="http://wiki.l-functions.org/LfunctionsAndModularFormsII/CentralValues/Rank4">LfunctionsAndModularFormsII / CentralValues / Rank4</a> [Broken link]
%o A194687 (PARI) r(n)=ellanalyticrank(ellinit([0,0,0,-n^2,0]))[1]
%o A194687 rec=0;for(n=1,1e4,t=r(n);if(t>rec,rec=t;print("r("n") = "t)))
%Y A194687 Cf. A062693, A062695, A003273, A309028, A309029, A319510.
%K A194687 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A194687 0,2
%A A194687 _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Sep 01 2011
%E A194687 Escape clause added to definition by _N. J. A. Sloane_, Jul 01 2024
%E A194687 a(7) from _Otakhon U. Kenjaev_, Sep 29 2026
